Author: William Theesfeld <william@theesfeld.net>
Date:   Mon Apr 6 11:35:27 2026 -0400

    fix(pipewire): use QPointer to prevent use-after-free on node removal
    
    When a PipeWire node is removed (e.g. Bluetooth headphones disconnect),
    the PwNodeIface is deleted synchronously via the destroying signal. If a
    deferred QML binding re-evaluation then calls setNode(), it attempts to
    QObject::disconnect() from the dangling mNode pointer, causing a SIGSEGV.
    
    Replace raw PwNodeIface* with QPointer<PwNodeIface> in PwAudioSpectrum,
    PwNodeLinkTracker, and PwNodePeakMonitor so the pointer auto-nulls when
    the object is destroyed, and existing null guards correctly skip the
    disconnect.

